  "narrative": "Starting from a market-based anchor around 0.65 for turnover, a high-impact event (death) plus established succession mechanisms and domestic/external pressures yield a calibrated posterior near 0.95 for Khamenei ceasing to be supreme leader before 1 April 2026. The estimate incorporates both strong signals and modest caveats from potential misreports and structural changes.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.65,
      "basis": "reference-class anchor drawn from near-term prediction-market forecasts of leadership turnover in Iran within 2026, reflecting multiple sources estimating mid-60s odds prior to the window."
    },
    "factor_updates": [
      {
        "factor": "Death of Ali Khamenei (Feb 28, 2026)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Credible outlets reported Khamenei's death on Feb 28, 2026, instantly vacating the post and triggering succession processes, dramatically increasing turnover probability."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Institutional succession mechanism (Assembly of Experts / provisional leadership council)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Constitutional procedures provide a pathway to a swift turnover after vacancy, accelerating near-term changes."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Economic crisis and mass protests driving demand for change",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Worsening economy and unrest underpin sustained pressure for leadership change within 2026."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Abolition of the Supreme Leader post (structural change) as a possible outcome",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Market signals include tail-risk that the office could be abolished, which would resolve the turnover question within the window."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Disinformation risk or conflicting death reports",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Although death reports were credible, the possibility of disputed narratives could temporarily dampen signals."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Regional crisis escalation and external pressure (US-Israel strikes, etc.)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "External shocks can hasten internal decision-making and accelerate leadership change."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Mojtaba Khamenei as likely successor (market signal)",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "weak",
        "rationale": "Markets often signal a plausible successor, aligning turnover with a defined post-change leadership path."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "Starting from the anchor around 0.65, a strong high-impact event (death) plus rapid succession mechanisms and ongoing crisis pressures jointly tilt the probability toward turnover. The combination of multiple independent up-deltas yields a calibrated, high-probability posterior (~0.95), while weak dampeners (disinformation risk and ambiguous succession sequencing) cap upside risk and preserve calibration within a narrow range."
  }
}

{
  "probability": 0.95,
  "range_low": 0.90,
